# check that changedsince filters out messages before 2180 4.1.* acts on
# the remaining set. A mailbox starts at nextmodseq 2, so the four
# appends take 2:5, the store 6, the expunge 7 and the last store 8.
depends 2180base
send 1
d fetch 1:* modseq
receive 5
* 1 FETCH (MODSEQ (2))
* 2 FETCH (MODSEQ (3))
* 3 FETCH (MODSEQ (4))
* 4 FETCH (MODSEQ (5))
d OK done
send 1
a store 1:2 +flags.silent \deleted
receive 1
a OK done
send 1
a uid expunge 1:2
receive 3
* 1 EXPUNGE
* 1 EXPUNGE
a OK done
# the expunge above took a modseq, so .silent no longer lines up with
# what this session has reported and we echo the store back. Sending
# too much is better than too little, so expect it.
send 1
a store 1 +flags.silent \deleted
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (UID 3 FLAGS (\Deleted \Recent))
a OK done
use watcher
send 1
c fetch 1:3 (uid body.peek[header.fields (date)])
# this session is never told that main set \Deleted on UID 3 - see
# zeromodseq, which is about that and still fails. It is beside the
# point here, so do not expect it.
receive 5
* 3 FETCH (UID 3 BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (Date)] {41}
Date: Thu, 27 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

)
c NO UID(s) 1,2 has/have been expunged
send 1
c fetch 1:3 (uid body.peek[header.fields (date)]) (changedsince 8)
# MSN 3 has MS 8, so the changedsince filters out the only message we
# could have returned. 1:2 are still expunged, so 4.1.2 still applies,
# and asking a second time after being told earns the CLIENTBUG bye.
receive 3
* BYE [CLIENTBUG] These messages have been expunged: 1,2
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
c NO UID(s) 1,2 has/have been expunged
end
